    "method": "For each of the 350 RDKit-canonical-SMILES-distinct corpus structures, compute rdkit.Chem.inchi.MolToInchiKey and group by key. A group with >1 member is a duplicate structure the canonical-SMILES dedup did not catch (InChI's mobile-H layer normalizes tautomer pairs -- lactam/lactim, 1H/2H-tetrazole, 2-pyridone/2-hydroxypyridine, etc -- that RDKit's canonical SMILES leaves as distinct strings because the formal bonding differs).",
