    "root_cause": "cap() = s.replace('*','C'), used identically by R-A07/V-A07/R-A07v2/W-NOV1/this script, does not normalize atom-mapped wildcard dummy-atom notation. Some OpenPoly PSMILES rows for a repeat unit use bare '*' end-groups, others use atom-mapped '[*:1]'/'[*:2]' end-groups for the SAME polymer under a second display name (e.g. 'PDMS' vs 'Polydimethylsiloxane (PDMS)'; 'PE' vs 'High-density polyethylene (HDPE)'). Naive string replacement turns '[*:1]' into '[C:1]' (an atom-mapped carbon, not a plain methyl cap), so the two notations canonicalize to two different RDKit SMILES strings and both survive canonical-SMILES dedup as if distinct. InChIKey ignores atom-map numbers and correctly identifies them as the same repeat-unit structure.",
